  "answer": "Following Nvidia's strong quarterly performance, a wave of analyst upgrades ensued. Analysts from Bank of America, Goldman Sachs, and Citi all raised their price targets on NVDA, with Goldman Sachs and Citi also upgrading the stock to \"Buy\" ratings. Specifically, Goldman Sachs' Toshiya Hari raised the price target to $165.00, citing data center demand strength and confirmation of Blackwell ramp, while Citi's Atif Malik increased his price target to $175.00, noting that Q4 guidance exceeded expectations by 15% for fiscal year 2026 estimates. Bank of America's Vivek Arya maintained a \"Buy\" rating but raised the price target to $190.00, emphasizing the Blackwell cycle as a multi-year AI infrastructure tailwind.\n\nSources used:\n- [Source: rating-nvda-002]\n- [Source: rating-nvda-001]\n- [Source: rating-nvda-004]\n- [Source: rating-nvda-003]",
